        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "da425e59-08f6-3918-8231-550abb0982d0",
                "word": "barkhane",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1a27dc21-2078-4da4-a87f-95805b76bbd7",
                        "entry_id": "da425e59-08f6-3918-8231-550abb0982d0",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "barkhanes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7980db71-5c9b-3861-9a38-362c75cfc83b",
                        "entry_id": "da425e59-08f6-3918-8231-550abb0982d0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dune créée par la saltation du sable sous l’action du vent."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7cd952fc-851d-46d4-8c5e-062705c8d97f",
                                "sense_id": "7980db71-5c9b-3861-9a38-362c75cfc83b",
                                "text": "La barkhane graduellement surélevée dévie les flux particulaires vers les bords où les sables s’accumulent en une double traîne formant les « ailes » ou les « cornes » de la dune en croissant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f459fab-fbd7-44ca-a541-db3a2a81018c",
                                "sense_id": "7980db71-5c9b-3861-9a38-362c75cfc83b",
                                "text": "Le désert, au contraire, sauf quand le vent s'éveille, est un océan minéral et figé, un océan avec ses hautes lames, ses vagues en demi-lune, les barkhane – dunes de sable effilées comme un yatagan, le sabre turc -, une immensité désolée de rocs, de sel et de poussière d'où émane une fascinante beauté : celle de la nudité parfaite, celle d'un monde réduit à l'essentiel, un univers de dureté et de violence."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c9bebbf1-cdbf-448c-8e4f-f4839e3f1d18",
                        "source_entry_id": "da425e59-08f6-3918-8231-550abb0982d0",
                        "source_sense_id": "7980db71-5c9b-3861-9a38-362c75cfc83b",
                        "target_lang_word": "barchan",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "barchan",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8aae2150-c651-3e05-b5d3-4b23053b541c",
                                        "entry_id": "4fb731d7-9d86-3dca-8965-834b97c7889b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An arc-shaped shifting sand dune comprising well-sorted (uniformly sized) sand."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "also",
                                            "attributive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7816d5d9-168a-4e18-a8c6-0462133e0358",
                                                "sense_id": "8aae2150-c651-3e05-b5d3-4b23053b541c",
                                                "text": "The sand is usually very well sorted in barchans, for it is constantly re-worked as the dune 'marches'. The marching also causes cross-bedding inside the barchan, with a dip parallel to the sand-fall face."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d09aa8c3-578a-484f-8d75-b0401281a8e3",
                                                "sense_id": "8aae2150-c651-3e05-b5d3-4b23053b541c",
                                                "text": "But to follow the dunes around the foot of their slopes is also tedious and one can walk for half a kilometre east or west, finding one barchan linked to another and no easy way through, and the unverifiable suspicion grows that one has been driven by insensible curves actually southwards."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "518c080e-3560-415d-99c1-eea612dab7d2",
                                                "sense_id": "8aae2150-c651-3e05-b5d3-4b23053b541c",
                                                "text": "The structure out here was revealed immediately—desert punctuated by oases in a geography of cruelty, barkhans or traveling sand-dunes a hundred feet high, which might or might not possess consciousness, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f80d7af7-9d4e-471a-a7c6-20cd82b20aae",
                                                "sense_id": "8aae2150-c651-3e05-b5d3-4b23053b541c",
                                                "text": "Barchans and transverse dunes are essentially of the same type, forming and migrating under a unidirectional wind regime. The difference between the two is related to the amount of sand: barchans are isolated mounds, whereas transverse dunes are composed of many barchans coalesced into a single, longer dune form[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c019233-8f9e-4e91-bb12-d90aaa00ca43",
                                                "sense_id": "8aae2150-c651-3e05-b5d3-4b23053b541c",
                                                "text": "Perhaps the most distinctive is the barchan dune, an isolated crescentic form with arms that stretch downwind. Barchans are not huge, often with heights of only a few meters."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
